me><given-names>YS</given-names></name><name><surname>Jyothi</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhaskar</surname><given-names>VS</given-names></name><name><surname>Dandona</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The lack of public health research output from India</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><year>2004</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>55</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15563377</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2458-4-55</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><source>World Health Statistics 2008</source><year>2008</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/whosis/whostat/2008/en/index.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><article-title>Global burden of disease estimates: Death and DALY estimates for 2002 by cause for WHO member states</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/healthinfo/global_burden_disease/en/index.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lopez</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathers</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezzati</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamison</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>CJL</given-names></name><collab>(Eds)</collab></person-group><source>Global Burden of Disease and Risk Factors</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Washington: The World Bank &#x00026; Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jamison</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Breman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Measham</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Alleyne</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Claeson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Jha</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Musgrove</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><collab>(Eds)</collab></person-group><source>Disease Control Priorities in Developing Countries</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Washington: The World Bank &#x00026; Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Omune</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk factors for the major causes of disease burden in India</article-title><source>Master of International Public Health (Honours) Thesis</source><year>2008</year><publisher-name>Sydney; University of Sydney, School of Public Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Registrar General and Census Commissioner</collab></person-group><article-title>Census of India</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.censusindia.gov.in/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Raut</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><source>Mortality Statistics in I